From c762ef2620d749cc78192624df31b7075573878e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ant=C3=B3nio=20Sarmento?= <Keyaku@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 15:38:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] FuseDaemon: fall back to current-time setattr when explicit
 times hit EPERM

On public volumes (vfat/exfat) vold mounts the backing filesystem with a
fixed owner uid (root), so the daemon has group write access but is not
the file owner. With the writeback cache enabled the kernel flushes its
cached mtime as a FUSE_SETATTR with explicit times before FLUSH/FSYNC,
and explicit-time utimensat()/futimens() require ownership or
CAP_FOWNER. The resulting EPERM is returned by the kernel from every
close() and fsync() after a write, making apps believe their writes
failed even though the data landed.

Retry with NULL times, i.e. both timestamps set to the current time:
the VFS waives the owner check only when every timestamp is UTIME_NOW
(a partial UTIME_NOW/UTIME_OMIT mix is still owner-checked), and only
write permission is then required. The timestamp flush immediately
follows the write, so the resulting mtime is essentially correct, and
these filesystems cannot represent per-file ownership anyway, so the
EPERM is structural rather than a real denial.

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I37d1b2dd4a772182529afad0b4c90cf1a5e0673e
---
 jni/FuseDaemon.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/jni/FuseDaemon.cpp b/jni/FuseDaemon.cpp
index 7dc629f..7f17048 100644
--- a/jni/FuseDaemon.cpp
+++ b/jni/FuseDaemon.cpp
@@ -706,6 +706,21 @@ static void pf_setattr(fuse_req_t req,
             res = futimens(fd, times);
         }
 
+        if (res < 0 && errno == EPERM) {
+            // Public volumes (vfat/exfat) are mounted with a fixed owner uid, so
+            // setting explicit timestamps fails the VFS owner check for the daemon
+            // even though it has write access. This turns every close()/fsync()
+            // into EPERM once the kernel flushes its writeback-cached mtime.
+            // Retry with NULL times (both set to now): the VFS only waives the
+            // owner check when every timestamp is UTIME_NOW, and the flush
+            // follows the write immediately, so "now" is accurate.
+            if (fd == -1) {
+                res = utimensat(-1, path.c_str(), nullptr, 0);
+            } else {
+                res = futimens(fd, nullptr);
+            }
+        }
+
         if (res < 0) {
             fuse_reply_err(req, errno);
             return;
